<p>Click to Enlarge Memorial Highway was widened to five lanes. Rear-end collisions were the frequent result of high traffic volumes on a two-lane road. The $1.2 million project provided a central turning lane and and lighting, a train underpass and river levee gate on the west end access to Mandan Avenue. The project also removed hundreds elm and box-elder trees, planted in the mid-1920s by the Mandan's Daughters of American Revolution and American Legion Auxillary.</p>
